  "text": "proprium.septem-dolorum-beatae-mariae-virginis-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Seven Sorrows of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": {
      "translation": "The Lord has blessed you by His power, Who by you has brought our enemies to nought. Blessed are you, O daughter, by the Lord the Most High God, above all women upon the earth. Blessed be the Lord Who made heaven and earth, because He has so magnified your name this day, that your praise shall not depart out of the mouth of men, who shall be mindful of the power of the Lord forever: for you have not spared your life by reason of the distress and tribulation of your people, but have prevented our ruin in the presence of our God."
    }
  },
